      "text": "To simplify the expression \\((1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ)\\), we will use the tangent addition formula and some trigonometric identities. Let's proceed step by step.\n\nFirst, recall the tangent addition formula:\n\\[\n\\tan(A + B) = \\frac{\\tan A + \\tan B}{1 - \\tan A \\tan B}\n\\]\n\nWe need to find a relationship between \\(\\tan 20^\\circ\\) and \\(\\tan 25^\\circ\\) using this formula. Let's set \\(A = 20^\\circ\\) and \\(B = 25^\\circ\\). Then we have:\n\\[\n\\tan(A + B) = \\tan 45^\\circ\n\\]\nWe know that:\n\\[\n\\tan 45^\\circ = 1\n\\]\n\nUsing the tangent addition formula, we get:\n\\[\n1 = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ}\n\\]\n\nNow, let's denote:\n\\[\nx = \\tan 20^\\circ \\quad \\text{and} \\quad y = \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThus, the equation becomes:\n\\[\n1 = \\frac{x + y}{1 - xy}\n\\]\n\nRearranging this equation, we get:\n\\[\n1 - xy = x + y\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\n1 = x + y + xy\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to express \\(x + y\\) in terms of \\(\\tan 20^\\circ\\) and \\(\\tan 25^\\circ\\). To do this, we use the tangent subtraction formula. Recall that:\n\\[\n\\tan(45^\\circ - 5^\\circ) = \\tan 40^\\circ\n\\]\n\nUsing the tangent subtraction formula, we get:\n\\[\n\\tan(45^\\circ - 5^\\circ) = \\frac{\\tan 45^\\circ - \\tan 5^\\circ}{1 + \\tan 45^\\circ \\tan 5^\\circ}\n\\]\n\nSince \\(\\tan 45^\\circ = 1\\), this simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\tan 40^\\circ = \\frac{1 - \\tan 5^\\circ}{1 + \\tan 5^\\circ}\n\\]\n\nWe also know that:\n\\[\n\\tan 5^\\circ = \\tan(20^\\circ - 15^\\circ) = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ - \\tan 15^\\circ}{1 + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 15^\\circ}\n\\]\n\nHowever, a simpler approach is to use the known fact that:\n\\[\n\\tan 40^\\circ = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + 1 / \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\cdot 1 / \\tan 25^\\circ}\n\\]\n\nBy simplifying this, we find:\n\\[\n\\tan 40^\\circ = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ}\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\\[\n1 = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ}\n\\]\n\nMultiplying both sides by \\(1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\\), we get:\n\\[\n1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ = \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\n\nRearranging terms, we have:\n\\[\n1 = x + y + xy\n\\]\n\nWe need to simplify:\n\\[\n(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ)\n\\]\n\nUsing the identity \\((a + b)(c + d) = ac + ad + bc + bd\\), we get:\n\\[\n(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) = 1 \\cdot 1 + \\tan 20^\\circ \\cdot 1 + 1 \\cdot \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\cdot \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\n\nSimplifying further:\n\\[\n= 1 + \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\n\nFrom earlier steps, we know:\n\\[\n1 = x + y + xy\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\\[\n= 1 + 1 + xy\n\\]\n\nSince \\(xy = \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\\), and we have already established that:\n\\[\n1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ = \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final simplified form is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{4}\n\\]",
