      "text": "To solve the problem \\((1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ)\\), we will use trigonometric identities and properties. Let's break it down step by step.\n\nFirst, let's denote \\( \\theta = \\tan 20^\\circ \\) and \\( \\phi = \\tan 25^\\circ \\). We need to find the value of \\( (1 + \\theta)(1 + \\phi) \\).\n\nWe can start by expanding the expression:\n\\[\n(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) = 1 + \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nNext, we use the tangent addition formula, but in a different form that fits our needs. Recall the identity:\n\\[\n\\tan(45^\\circ - x) = \\frac{1 - \\tan x}{1 + \\tan x}.\n\\]\nThis can be rearranged to:\n\\[\n\\tan(45^\\circ - x) \\tan(45^\\circ + x) = \\tan(45^\\circ - (45^\\circ - x)) = \\tan x.\n\\]\nSo,\n\\[\n\\tan(45^\\circ - x) \\tan(45^\\circ + x) = 1.\n\\]\n\nWe can apply this identity to \\( \\theta \\) and \\( \\phi \\):\n\\[\n\\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 65^\\circ = 1.\n\\]\nWe know that \\( 65^\\circ = 45^\\circ - 20^\\circ \\) and \\( 85^\\circ = 45^\\circ + 40^\\circ \\), but we don't need these angles specifically. Instead, we can use the fact that \\( \\tan 25^\\circ \\) and \\( \\tan 65^\\circ \\) are involved, and we need their product.\n\nHowever, a more straightforward approach is to use the identity for the product of tangent functions when the angles are such that their sum is a right angle plus a certain angle. Let's consider:\n\\[\n\\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ = \\tan 45^\\circ.\n\\]\nThis identity simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ + (\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ) = 1.\n\\]\nThus, we can rewrite the original expression as:\n\\[\n(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) = 1 + \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ.\n\\]\nUsing the identity \\(\\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ + (\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ) = 1\\), we have:\n\\[\n(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) = 1 + 1 = 2.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}.\n\\]",
